    "description": "Coastal GasLink is a long-haul natural gas transmission pipeline connecting northeastern British Columbia supply to the LNG Canada export facility near Kitimat. Its end market is LNG export and related upstream gas production, with transportation services supporting feedgas delivery from the Western Canadian Sedimentary Basin. The operating model is asset-heavy and infrastructure based, with value derived from long-life pipeline transportation under contracted or utility-style tolling arrangements rather than asset-light services. Public materials describe an approximately 670-kilometre pipeline across northern British Columbia that entered commercial service and is positioned to support LNG Canada. TC Energy announced in 2019 that it would sell a combined 65% equity interest in the project to KKR and AIMCo while retaining 35%, and 2024 Coastal GasLink materials continued to describe the project as owned by affiliates of those three parties.",
